{
  "kanji": "色",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 色\ntitle: color\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 6\nradical: 色\nradicalNumber: 139\nonyomi: [ショク, シキ]\nkunyomi: [いろ]\ndistractors: [白, 急, 魚]\n---\n\n# 色 — color\n\n**Strokes:** 6 · **Key (radical):** 色 (no. 139) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n色 names color, rather than one particular color. In some words it extends to appearance or a distinctive character.\nFor the everyday noun, learn [色](../words/色.md) いろ.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the upper strokes as a paintbrush poised above a curled pot of color.\nThis is a memory aid for the modern outline, not a historical explanation.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| いろ | kun | [色](../words/色.md) いろ — color; 茶色 ちゃいろ — brown |\n| ショク | on | 特色 とくしょく — distinctive feature |\n| シキ | on | 景色 けしき — scenery; 色彩 しきさい — color |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [色](../words/色.md) いろ — color\n- 茶色 ちゃいろ — brown\n- 景色 けしき — scenery\n- 特色 とくしょく — distinctive feature\n\n## Notes\n\n[白](白.md) and [青](青.md) name particular colors; 色 is the category.\n茶色 combines [茶](茶.md) チャ with native いろ, so it is not an on+on reading.\nLearn 景色 as けしき without treating け as a freely reusable reading of 景.\n",
